{"reviews":[{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0097","row_sha256":"3012e7aee9af338ee85b61c2a763835343cd6ff7ee15e62d09b062042dbdabfb","critique":"The output fixes capitalization and smooths phrasing well. "On Tuesdays" fits the recurring meeting, and "along the canal," "ran with," and "big deal of it" are acceptable polish. All facts are preserved: six months, 6:30, four miles, three weeks, two missed Tuesdays and Mara. The hedges and the closing question are also kept.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0102","row_sha256":"2e22c9ab1f251799d349beb01012962442f3366132e728676eecb91ba38a1e13","critique":"This is an identity row, and the output is byte-identical to the already clean input. The date, time, location and instructions are unchanged.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0089","row_sha256":"3da35638226806d5742ed29f52f78ea7040c56d91ab1a02070117cf59a0a3fb3","critique":"Checked paragraph by paragraph. All proposals and details are retained:
- the six-week trial and the weekend-only fallback;
- the Sunday 10 a.m. example;
- the three washer columns;
- the line-through convention;
- the six racks, two of them near the sink, and the quoted note text;
- washer two's slow draining and Marisol;
- the three-item outline;
- the two volunteers;
- the first-Monday start;
- the ten-minute review.
Hedges such as "I don't know whether" and "I'm not sure this happens often" are preserved. The rewordings ("consider," "a line," "helpful," "change the wording") do not alter meaning.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0103","row_sha256":"676a1cf48bea3a52558be4b0070ba50f9775dc0e034dbfbb807db92ab1ff804a","critique":"The output corrects capitalization. Changing "the same things" to "the same faces" is a reasonable stylistic fit, since the list is all people. The 7:18 train, last winter and the three described commuters are all preserved.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0104","row_sha256":"a43028f6d9b1fa9c92c12c678c362b85976799f1714e53be113c6d91b0a88ef8","critique":"German capitalization is corrected and the long sentence is split cleanly. "Bei voller Fahrt" becomes "wenn der Zug voll ist," which matches the intended crowding meaning given "eng." The three weeks, Lindenau to Mitte, punctuality, quiet announcements and the overall assessment are preserved.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0105","row_sha256":"6f2d4a1afbe0b1f1f6ed5f40eede993296491b3ce9cbc3a5e7fe602cead8f3e0","critique":"The output capitalizes the names Nora and Leeds. It also fixes the awkward "that neither of us was understanding" to "which neither of us could understand." The 6:20 train, last Tuesday and the board check are preserved.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0107","row_sha256":"4d6fb91857e7e03dcb316f1c3d33d888c06d581a8743dc7ae19410bca3d8f45c","critique":"This is an identity row, and the output is byte-identical to the polished input. The 7:40 train, the clock meeting spot and the one-week trial are unchanged.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0108","row_sha256":"f29a435220297829f503f5c053bb70d0c9a161b83bf53c4ff478454844442b14","critique":"Station and destination names are capitalized. All details are preserved:
- the closure times and date;
- the platform reassignments for Elm Park and Central Market;
- the lift limitations;
- staff assistance and the ten extra minutes;
- no replacement buses and valid tickets;
- the conditional possibility of an extension.
